SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade Oct
 ober Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade October Payme
 nt Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations\nAttention Trading Partners
 : MIHMS Upgrade October Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitation
 s\nSep 21\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, the Office of MaineCare 
 Services (OMS) is preparing to launch an upgraded version of MIHMS\, Maine
 Care’s claims processing system. The upgrade is currently scheduled to g
 o live on October 10\, 2026. To support a smooth transition\, OMS must imp
 lement temporary system access limitations and adjustments to payment cycl
 es in October.\nFrom Friday\, October 2 at 8:00 PM until Monday\, October 
 12 at 8:00 AM\, MIHMS will be in a “data freeze” while OMS completes f
 inal system readiness and transition activities.\nPlease note that we have
  updated the\nFAQ\npreviously shared\, as of September 21\, 2026.\nChanges
  to October payment cycles:\nReview this information and plan billing acco
 rdingly to prepare for the transition.\nPayment Cycle Date\nType of Cycle\
 nClaim Submission Deadline for Inclusion in Payment Cycle*\nWednesday\, 9/
 30/26\nLast regular payment cycle before the data freeze\nFriday\, 9/25/26
 \, 5:00 AM\nThursday\, 10/1/26\nExtra payment cycle before the data freeze
 \nWednesday\, 9/30/26\, 5:00 AM\nThere will be no payment on Wednesday\, O
 ctober 7.\nThursday\, 10/15/26\nFirst payment cycle after data freeze\, in
  upgraded system\nSecure File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) submission: Continu
 ous through data freeze up to Tuesday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nPortal submiss
 ion:\nBefore data freeze: Friday\, 10/2/26\, 7:59 PM\nAfter data freeze: T
 uesday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nWednesday\, 10/21/26\nRegular payment cycle\,
  in upgraded system\nFriday\, 10/16/26\, 5:00 AM\n*As always\, timely subm
 ission does not guarantee that the claim will process in time for the next
  payment cycle. OMS may take up to 30 days to process and pay a claim\, de
 pending on any edits or issue\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/pr
 ovider-bulletins/attention-trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-october-payment-
 cycle-changes-and-system-access-3
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-october-payment-cycle-changes-and-system-ac
 cess-3
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
