DTSTAMP:20260918T043934Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine Dept. of Labor News and Updates - Septe
 mber 2026
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Maine Dept. 
 of Labor News and Updates - September 2026\nServices\nJobs & Training\nUne
 mployment Insurance\nDisability Services\nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLa
 bor Statistics\nWorkforce Development\nMaine Dept. of Labor News and Updat
 es - September 2026\nSeptember 17\, 2026\nMaine Dept. of Labor News and Up
 dates - September 2026\nYour monthly update from the Maine Department of L
 abor\, featuring announcements\, hiring events\, safety trainings\, worksh
 ops\, reports\, resources\, and opportunities for employers\, jobseekers a
 nd others interested in Maine's workforce.\nState offices are closed: Mon\
 , Oct 12 in observance of Indigenous Peoples Day\nANNOUNCEMENTS\nDeaf Cult
 ure Week\nMaine Commission for the Deaf\, Hard of Hearing and Late Deafene
 d (CDHHLD) hosts its 35th Annual Tea on\nSeptember 17 from 2 to 4 p.m.\nat
  the State House\, kicking off Deaf Culture Week\, which Governor Mills ha
 s proclaimed\nSeptember 20-26\n. The event celebrates Deaf culture and the
  heritage of American Sign Language\, while highlighting MDOL's commitment
  through the Bureau of Rehabilitation Services to advancing employment\, i
 ndependence\, and community integration for Mainers who are deaf or hard o
 f hearing.\nMore Information on the Division for the Deaf\, Hard of Hearin
 g and Late Deafened\n.\n~\nCompetitive Skills Scholarship Program Rules Up
 dated\nThe Maine Department of Labor has updated the Competitive Skills Sc
 holarship Program (CSSP) rules to reflect recent statutory changes\, expan
 d participant supports\, and increase flexibility.\nThe revised rules took
  effect on August 2\, 2026\n.\nMDOL is seeking input on the CSSP cohort mo
 del at listening sessions on\nSeptember 18: 10 a.m. virtual or 2:30 p.m. i
 n person\nat 45 Commerce\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.s
 html?id=13362368
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13362368
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
