SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: Training for New 
 MaineCare Partner Portal
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: Training for New MaineCare 
 Partner Portal\nAttention Trading Partners: Training for New MaineCare Par
 tner Portal\nSep 08\, 2026\nWe have\npreviously shared\nthat a refreshed a
 nd upgraded MIHMS\, with a new “MaineCare Partner Portal\,” is coming 
 in October 2026. This will replace the current HealthPAS Online Portal. 
 We are now inviting trading partners to\nregister for training that begin
 s September 8\, 2026\nto help you prepare for the transition to the new 
 portal. Trading partners include providers\, billing agents\, health plan
 s\, clearinghouses\, and business associates. Trading partners have an im
 portant role to play in supporting a smooth transition and uninterrupted 
 access to the portal after go-live.\nGainwell Technologies will be leadin
 g live virtual instructor-led training sessions. These courses will provid
 e the knowledge and skills needed to navigate the new portal\, complete da
 ily business functions\, and use new portal features. Training demonstrati
 ons\, materials\, and supporting resources will help participants prepare 
 for a successful transition.\nSteps you need to take to attend training\nR
 eview the available training topics listed below and identify the sessio
 ns that align with your role and responsibilities.\nUse the LMS registrati
 on (instructions below) to create an account\, access the training catalog
 \, and enroll in applicable sessions.\nContact Gainwell (instructions belo
 w) if you need assistance.\nRecorded sessions and other training material
 s will be available in the LMS after training sessions for ongoing referen
 ce.\nMaineCare Partner Portal Training Sessions\nCourse Name\nDescription\
 nME - TPT - Migrated Trading Partner Log In and Account Maintenance Trai
 ning (ILC)\nLearn how to complete first-time login activities\, configure 
 multi-factor authentication (MFA)\, manage user accounts and permissions\,
  perform accou\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletin
 s/attention-trading-partners-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-09
 -08
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-09-08
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:58a7fb92fd78386e@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260908T163659Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade Oct
 ober Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade October Payme
 nt Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations\nAttention Trading Partners
 : MIHMS Upgrade October Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitation
 s\nSep 08\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, the Office of MaineCare 
 Services (OMS) is preparing to launch an upgraded version of MIHMS\, Main
 eCare’s claims processing system. The upgrade is currently scheduled to
  go live on October 10\, 2026. To support a smooth transition\, OMS must i
 mplement temporary system access limitations and adjustments to payment cy
 cles in October.\nFrom Friday\, October 2 at 8:00 PM until Monday\, Octobe
 r 12 at 8:00 AM\, MIHMS will be in a “data freeze” while OMS completes
  final system readiness and transition activities.\nPlease note that we ha
 ve updated the\nFAQ\npreviously shared\, as of September 8\, 2026.\nChan
 ges to October payment cycles:\nReview this information and plan billing a
 ccordingly to prepare for the transition.\nPayment Cycle Date\nType of Cyc
 le\nClaim Submission Deadline for Inclusion in Payment Cycle*\nWednesday\,
  9/30/26\nLast regular payment cycle before the data freeze\nFriday\, 9/
 25/26\, 5:00 AM\nThursday\, 10/1/26\nExtra\npayment cycle before the dat
 a freeze\nWednesday\, 9/30/26\, 5:00 AM\nThere will be no payment on Wedne
 sday\, October 7.\nThursday\, 10/15/26\nFirst payment cycle after data f
 reeze\, in upgraded system\nSecure File Transfer Protocol (SFTP) submissio
 n: Continuous through data freeze up to Tuesday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nPort
 al submission:\nBefore data freeze: Friday\, 10/2/26\, 7:59 PM\nAfter data
  freeze: Tuesday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nWednesday\, 10/21/26\nRegular payme
 nt cycle\, in upgraded system\nFriday\, 10/16/26\, 5:00 AM\n*As always\,
  timely submission does not guarantee that the claim will process in tim
 e for the next payment cycle. OMS may take up to 30 days to process and pa
 y a claim\, depending on any edits or issues\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/o
 ms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-o
 ctober-payment-cycle-changes-and-system-access-1
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-october-payment-cycle-changes-and-system-ac
 cess-1
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4b17db0d73e88aa6@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260904T204459Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Looking Ahead: Eligibility-Dedicated Data Fee
 d to Support MaineCare Renewals and Enrollment
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Looking Ahead: Eligibility-Dedicated Data Feed to Suppo
 rt MaineCare Renewals and Enrollment\nLooking Ahead: Eligibility-Dedicated
  Data Feed to Support MaineCare Renewals and Enrollment\nSep 04\, 2026\nTw
 o weeks ago\, we\nannounced\ncommunications support for MaineCare partners
  and providers regarding changes the federal government is making to Maine
 Care (Maine’s Medicaid program) eligibility. This message provides an ea
 rly look at planned data-sharing that will help the Maine Department of He
 alth and Human Services (DHHS) verify information needed for MaineCare eli
 gibility. Our goal is to help eligible Mainers keep their coverage and acc
 ess to services with as little disruption as possible.\nNo action is neede
 d now.\nWe are sharing this information early to make providers aware of w
 hat is being planned. We will share more information as plans and timeline
 s are finalized.\nDHHS will continue to use administrative data sources it
  has access to as much as possible to support automatic (“passive”) re
 newals for MaineCare members. Federal changes to eligibility mean we need 
 additional information to help more eligible members maintain their MaineC
 are coverage. This data will help Mainers continue to benefit from MaineCa
 re\, which in turn will help providers minimize the impact of these federa
 l Medicaid cuts on their revenue and on their charity and uncompensated ca
 re.\nClinical Data Will Help People Stay Enrolled in MaineCare\nElectronic
  health record (EHR) systems contain clinical data that Maine and numerous
  other states are planning to use to help\nexempt\nMedicaid applicants and
  members with work-limiting health conditions from Work Requirements. In M
 aine\, this data will\nsupport MaineCare eligibility determination activit
 ies administered by the Office for Family Independence (OFI)\n. DHHS inten
 ds to partner with\nproviders to collect this information th\nhttps://www.
 maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/looking-ahead-eligibility-
 dedicated-data-feed-support-mainecare-renewals-and-enrollment
